{
 "definition": "Same-class negatives scoring of the residue edge head on the 800 PINDER validation complexes (negatives-v1, 2026-10-29).\n\nExtends score_decoy.py (imported: validation set, LAYOUT, logits, retype arm, seeds) with the stratum / UniProt handling and\nthe wrong-partner control of decoy-rank-v1's check_similarity.py. Free branch only, selected checkpoint per selection.json,\nCPU jax. Receptor = chain code 0, partner = chain code 1; surface = free RSA >= 0.1; contact pairs C_i = receptor-surface x\npartner-surface pairs with soft target > 0.5; pair score = sigmoid(edge logit). Pairwise accuracy: true beats decoy, ties 1/2.\nStratum = pool-v4 pinder-val.tsv (hetero / homo / Ab/Ag); UniProt per chain code from the PINDER id (check_similarity.py).\n  (a) re-typed: score_decoy.py arm (1), unchanged.\n  (b) same-stratum swapped partner: 5 decoy complexes j per i with stratum(j) == stratum(i), j != i, and j not carrying i's\n      partner UniProt (when defined); decoy = mean over C_i of score(a, b'), b' drawn (fixed seed, with replacement) from\n      j's contact residues on j's partner side. Ab/Ag role matching: when i and j each have exactly one UNDEFINED-UniProt\n      chain (taken as the antibody), b' comes from j's chain with the role of i's partner (antibody for antibody), else\n      from j's chain code 1. Rows: all, hetero, homo, Ab/Ag (Ab/Ag-vs-Ab/Ag is a gate).\n  (c) surface-only same-stratum: true = mean over every receptor-surface x partner-surface pair of i; decoy = receptor\n      surface of i x surface of j's partner-role chain, j = the first of i's partners in (b).\n  (d) wrong-partner controls (check_similarity.py (4), hetero, surface-only score, receptor = chain code 0): B' = partner\n      chain of 5 random other hetero complexes whose partner UniProt differs (\"different protein\", gate), and B' = the\n      chain carrying B's UniProt in other hetero complexes (\"same UniProt, other complex\", up to 5). Extra Ab/Ag row with\n      role-matched complexes: receptor = antigen, B' = antibody chain of 5 other role-matched Ab/Ag complexes whose antigen\n      UniProt differs from i's (POISK-like wrong-antibody control).\n  (e) within-complex: anchors = interface residues (surface, a cross-chain partner <= 10 A; the training definition), with\n      at least one contact and one non-contact among the other chain's interface residues; per anchor AUROC (ties 1/2) of\n      contacts (<= 10 A) vs non-contact interface residues of the partner, and top-1 (highest-scoring candidate is a\n      contact); mean over anchors, overall and by stratum.\n  (f) edges: pooled AUROC / AP and macro AP of the true receptor x partner surface pairs, contact <= 10 A (score_decoy).\n  (g) curvature proxy (production_residue.curvature, free-branch graph, model-independent): mean on interface vs\n      non-interface surface residues, AUROC for interface among surface residues, Spearman with free RSA (all residues\n      with an RSA, and surface residues); per-residue values saved to curvature.npz.\n  pKa: clean selection (PINDER val state MAE + interface paired MAE without bonded-Cys sites) from the stored predictions\n      (score_residue.py's pka()).\n  python score_negatives.py OUT_DIR NAME=RUN [NAME=RUN ...]   (first NAME is the control printed beside the GATES)\n",
